# Deployment safety (T3Planet Docs)

## 🚨 Permission gate (non-negotiable)

**Default = LOCAL ONLY.** No `git push`, Mintlify production deploy, live DNS/domain changes, or production publish unless the operator says exactly:

```text
start the deployment process
```

Near-synonyms (`deploy`, `push live`, `release`, `finish`, `make it ready`, etc.) are **not** authorization. Do not ask to deploy — wait for the exact phrase.

Full gate: `.cursor/rules/deployment-permission-gate.mdc`.

When authorized, follow `docs/deployment/deploy.md` and `.cursor/skills/t3planet-deploy/SKILL.md`.

## Must (only after authorization)

1. Confirm the exact phrase was given; then inspect remote, branch, identity, and full diff.
2. Push only to `origin` → `nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs` (`master`) unless operator redirects.
3. Commit as **Nitsan** `<sanjay@nitsantech.com>` (author env OK; do not forge tokens; do not invent emails).
4. `git fetch` + compare before push; synchronize safely; never force-push `master`.
5. Stage an explicit file list; verify `git diff --cached --name-only`.
6. Re-verify Mintlify Git connection (org repo / `master`) before claiming live updated.
7. Run post-deploy live QA; report with evidence.
8. Use `NOT VERIFIED` when a check could not be done.

## Must not

1. Push or deploy without `start the deployment process`.
2. Force push.
3. Expose credentials, tokens, or `.env`.
4. Blind `git add .` / `git add -A`.
5. Stage, commit, push, or deploy **`docs-master/`** or **`workshops/`**.
6. Delete/reset those excluded trees.
7. Claim PASS from GitHub push alone.
8. Silently reconnect or rewrite Mintlify project settings.
9. Use a personal fork as the normal production Mintlify source.
10. **Delete, remove, or recreate** the Cloudflare custom hostname / custom domain for `docs.t3planet.de` to flush cache (breaks SSL — see `custom-domain-ssl-safety.mdc`).
11. Change production ACME / DCV DNS without an approved SSL recovery plan.
12. Auto-commit unless the operator explicitly asked to commit (commit ≠ push ≠ deploy).

Mintlify still on a personal fork while pushing org-only → live will lag; prefer reconnect, emergency same-SHA fork sync only if authorized and urgent (see `mintlify-deployment.mdc`).

Git commit identity ≠ GitHub authentication. Setting `user.name` does not grant push permission.
